{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-c30d9595ca4324e1d426","statement":"Let $V$ be a vertex algebra, $M$ a $V$-module.\nThe Poisson vertex algebra module structure of $\\gr^F M$\nrestricts to the Poisson module structure\nof $\\bar M:=M/F^1 M$ over $R_V$, that is,\n$\\bar M$ is a Poisson $R_V$-module by\n\n\\begin{align*}\n\\bar  a\\cdot \\bar m=\\overline{a_{(-1)}m},\\quad \\ad(\\bar a)(\\bar m)=\\overline{a_{(0)}m}.\n\\end{align*}","source_id":"arXiv:1605.00138","cluster":"representation_theory","statement_sha256":"6da1ac1d9d6f9b499d21403885e3ceb8a77c3c09ab25a36cbcf532848b356601","kind":"lemma","label":"Lemma 93","ref_key":"","name":"","order":120,"deps":[],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1605.00138","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"724ff59bda7dec23ea981e0821072acf559baccc91244b7151fe94c8b8c1233e","line":4140,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-27T22:13:42+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v2","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":342,"math_hints":37}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:1605.00138","title":"Introduction to W-algebras and their representation theory","abstract":"These are lecture notes from author's mini-course during Session 1: \"Vertex algebras, W-algebras, and application\" of INdAM Intensive research period \"Perspectives in Lie Theory\", at the Centro di Ricerca Matematica Ennio De Giorgi, Pisa, Italy. December 9, 2014 -- February 28, 2015.","authors":["Tomoyuki Arakawa"],"year":"2016","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1605.00138","cluster":"representation_theory","macros":{"tss":"\\hspace{1pt}","ts":"\\,","Caff":"{C}^{\\kappa}","Fock":"\\mc{F}","ch":"\\on{ch}","Mi":"\\Upupsilon","affQ":"\\hat Q_{(0)}","affn":"\\widehat{\\mf{n}}","affh":"\\widehat{\\mf{h}}","finn":"\\mf{n}","finb":"\\mf{b}","finh":"\\mf{h}","KL":"\\mathbf{KL}","bra":"{\\langle}","ket":"{\\rangle}","Lam":"\\Lambda","cprime":"$'$","on"